# Shared-domain rules

- Treat exported Zod schemas and types as API contracts consumed by both server and web.
- Represent calendar dates as `YYYY-MM-DD` day keys and instants as ISO timestamps.
- Use the shared time helpers for timezone and DST-safe calendar arithmetic.
- Keep four-week cycle behavior anchored to a Monday; week indexes are `0..3`, weekdays are `0=Sunday..6=Saturday`.
- Keep plan validation deterministic and side-effect free. Machine-readable issue codes are API surface.
- Add boundary tests for DST, cycle edges, invalid inputs, and deterministic sort order when relevant.
- Export new modules deliberately; prefer focused runtime subpath imports in the web app.
